{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-111214","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178839","text":"Retiring a lane — 2026-09-12"}]},{"id":"blk-111215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178840","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: a separate proposal, for a ruling. Nothing here is built, and it is deliberately not bundled with the review-limits work."}]},{"id":"blk-111216","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178841","text":"The gap, from a real lane"}]},{"id":"blk-111217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178842","text":"On 2026-09-12 "},{"id":"spn-178843","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/dogfood-setup.mjs"},{"id":"spn-178844","text":" opened lane "},{"id":"spn-178845","marks":["code"],"text":"ln_0016"},{"id":"spn-178846","text":" against "},{"id":"spn-178847","marks":["code"],"text":"ProjectAmp2/computedriven.com"},{"id":"spn-178848","text":" when the work was for "},{"id":"spn-178849","marks":["code"],"text":"ProjectAmp2/super"},{"id":"spn-178850","text":". The cause was the setup guessing ("},{"id":"spn-178851","marks":["code"],"text":"?? repos[0]"},{"id":"spn-178852","text":"), now fixed. What this proposal is about is what happened next: "},{"id":"spn-178853","marks":["bold"],"text":"nothing in the world could take that lane out of use."}]},{"id":"blk-111218","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178854","text":"There is no "},{"id":"spn-178855","marks":["code"],"text":"close_lane"},{"id":"spn-178856","text":", "},{"id":"spn-178857","marks":["code"],"text":"retire_lane"},{"id":"spn-178858","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-178859","marks":["code"],"text":"delete_lane"},{"id":"spn-178860","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-178861","marks":["code"],"text":"CommandSpec"},{"id":"spn-178862","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-111219","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178863","marks":["code"],"text":"delete_workspace"},{"id":"spn-178864","text":" refuses a workspace holding a lane —"}]}],"id":"blk-111221","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178865","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace-has-lanes"},{"id":"spn-178866","text":", "},{"id":"spn-178867","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Workspace deletion cannot remove established lanes or workers\""},{"id":"spn-178868","text":" — and the comment above it says lanes retain their ancestry."}]},{"id":"blk-111224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178869","marks":["bold"],"text":"That refusal is right and this proposal does not touch it."},{"id":"spn-178870","text":" A lane records that a bot was once permitted to work in a repository under a goal; deleting it would erase an authority decision that was really made. The gap is not that the history is kept. It is that "},{"id":"spn-178871","marks":["italic"],"text":"keeping the history"},{"id":"spn-178872","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-178873","marks":["italic"],"text":"still accepting new work"},{"id":"spn-178874","text":" are the same state."}]},{"id":"blk-111225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178875","text":"So "},{"id":"spn-178876","marks":["code"],"text":"ln_0016"},{"id":"spn-178877","text":" remains open: it can still be named by a new worker, a new plan, and a new worktree capability, and nothing on it says it was a mistake. The recovery had to re-create five plans on a correct lane and cancel the originals, and then leave the lane sitting there."}]},{"id":"blk-111226","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178878","text":"What is proposed"}]},{"id":"blk-111227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178879","text":"One transition on a field the record already has. A lane today:"}]},{"id":"blk-111228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178880","text":"%{\"id\" => \"ln_0016\", \"schema\" => \"lane@1\", \"status\" => \"open\", \"actor\" => …, \"goal_ref\" => …, \"repository_ref\" => …, \"workspace_ref\" => …}"}]},{"id":"blk-111229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178881","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-178882","text":" becomes "},{"id":"spn-178883","marks":["code"],"text":"open | retired"},{"id":"spn-178884","text":". Two human-control mutations, following the shape "},{"id":"spn-178885","marks":["code"],"text":"close_worker"},{"id":"spn-178886","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-178887","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen_worker"},{"id":"spn-178888","text":" already set:"}]},{"id":"blk-111230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178889","text":"retire_lane   lane_ref, reason      open → retired reopen_lane   lane_ref, reason      retired → open"}]},{"id":"blk-111231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178890","marks":["code"],"text":"reason"},{"id":"spn-178891","text":" is required and kept in the lane's history, because a retired lane with no reason is the same puzzle for the next reader that "},{"id":"spn-178892","marks":["code"],"text":"ln_0016"},{"id":"spn-178893","text":" is now."}]},{"id":"blk-111232","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178894","text":"What a retired lane must refuse, each by its own name"}]},{"id":"blk-111233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178895","text":"Not one predicate. A person who is told \"that lane is retired\" while trying to do four different things should be told which thing they were trying to do."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-111235","spans":[{"id":"spn-178896","text":"refused"}]},{"id":"blk-111236","spans":[{"id":"spn-178897","text":"because"}]}],"id":"blk-111234","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-111237","spans":[{"id":"spn-178898","marks":["code"],"text":"open_worker"},{"id":"spn-178899","text":" on it"}]},{"id":"blk-111238","spans":[{"id":"spn-178900","text":"new work in flight under a binding withdrawn on purpose"}]}],[{"id":"blk-111239","spans":[{"id":"spn-178901","marks":["code"],"text":"create_development_task"},{"id":"spn-178902","text":" on it"}]},{"id":"blk-111240","spans":[{"id":"spn-178903","text":"a new plan would inherit its "},{"id":"spn-178904","marks":["code"],"text":"repository_ref"}]}],[{"id":"blk-111241","spans":[{"id":"spn-178905","marks":["code"],"text":"record_development_attempt"},{"id":"spn-178906","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-178907","marks":["code"],"text":"record_development_change_set"},{"id":"spn-178908","text":" on a plan of its"}]},{"id":"blk-111242","spans":[{"id":"spn-178909","text":"review material would name a repository nobody means any more"}]}],[{"id":"blk-111243","spans":[{"id":"spn-178910","marks":["code"],"text":"accept_development_attempt"},{"id":"spn-178911","text":" on such a plan"}]},{"id":"blk-111244","spans":[{"id":"spn-178912","text":"acceptance writes to the repository the lane names — the one case where the binding is not merely descriptive"}]}],[{"id":"blk-111245","spans":[{"id":"spn-178913","marks":["code"],"text":"attach_worker"},{"id":"spn-178914","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-178915","marks":["code"],"text":"establish_worktree"},{"id":"spn-178916","text":" on it"}]},{"id":"blk-111246","spans":[{"id":"spn-178917","text":"a retired lane must not admit a "},{"id":"spn-178918","marks":["bold"],"text":"new worktree capability"},{"id":"spn-178919","text":"; this is the authority-bearing one"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-111247","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178920","text":"What must keep working, and this is the point"}]},{"id":"blk-111248","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178921","text":"Reading the lane, its goal, its actor, its repository, its plans, its"}]}],"id":"blk-111249","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111251","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178922","text":"attempts, its history. Retirement is a state, not a disappearance."}]},{"id":"blk-111252","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178923","marks":["code"],"text":"close_worker"},{"id":"spn-178924","text":" on a worker it already holds. Retiring a lane is a decision"}]}],"id":"blk-111253","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178925","text":"about the lane; closing a worker is a decision about work in flight."}]},{"id":"blk-111256","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178926","marks":["code"],"text":"update_development_task"},{"id":"spn-178927","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-178928","marks":["code"],"text":"cancelled"},{"id":"spn-178929","text":" on its plans, so a lane can be tidied"}]}],"id":"blk-111257","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178930","text":"after it is retired as well as before."}]},{"id":"blk-111260","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178931","text":"Existing active worktree capabilities keep whatever lifetime they already"}]}],"id":"blk-111261","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178932","text":"have. Retirement refuses "},{"id":"spn-178933","marks":["bold"],"text":"new"},{"id":"spn-178934","text":" authority; it is not a revocation, and dressing it up as one would make it a second, quieter "},{"id":"spn-178935","marks":["code"],"text":"revoke_grant"},{"id":"spn-178936","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-111264","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178937","text":"Two things to rule on"}]},{"id":"blk-111265","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178938","marks":["bold"],"text":"May a lane be retired while it still holds an open worker?"},{"id":"spn-178939","text":" Recommended:"}]}],"id":"blk-111266","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-111268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178940","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-178941","text":" — refuse "},{"id":"spn-178942","marks":["code"],"text":"lane-has-open-workers"},{"id":"spn-178943","text":" and name them, the way "},{"id":"spn-178944","marks":["code"],"text":"Workbench.choose"},{"id":"spn-178945","text":" refuses while a command is running. Retiring under a live worker would leave the worker holding a binding the world has withdrawn, and the alternative (retire and close them for you) makes one command do two decisions."}]},{"id":"blk-111269","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178946","marks":["bold"],"text":"Does a retired lane still block `delete_workspace`?"},{"id":"spn-178947","text":" Recommended:"}]}],"id":"blk-111270","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-111272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178948","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes, unchanged."},{"id":"spn-178949","text":" Retirement preserves ancestry; a workspace that held a lane still held it. Making retirement a route to deletion would reintroduce exactly what the existing refusal protects."}]},{"id":"blk-111273","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178950","text":"Not proposed"}]},{"id":"blk-111274","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178951","text":"Deleting a lane, or making "},{"id":"spn-178952","marks":["code"],"text":"delete_workspace"},{"id":"spn-178953","text":" more permissive."}]}],"id":"blk-111275","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178954","text":"Moving a lane to a different repository. A lane's repository is part of what"}]}],"id":"blk-111277","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178955","text":"the lane "},{"id":"spn-178956","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-178957","text":"; rebinding it would silently relabel every plan, attempt and capability already recorded against it. Retire it and open another."}]},{"id":"blk-111280","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-111282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178958","text":"Retiring anything automatically. A wrong binding is a judgement, and the"}]}],"id":"blk-111281","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-111283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178959","text":"reason field exists because a person has to make it."}]},{"id":"blk-111284","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178960","text":"Where this would be verified"}]},{"id":"blk-111285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178961","marks":["code"],"text":"ampd/test/"},{"id":"spn-178962","text":" for the transition and each refusal by name, plus a negative case per row of the table above; "},{"id":"spn-178963","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/sabotage-*.sh"},{"id":"spn-178964","text":" shape for making each refusal admit in turn, so a clause that stops refusing is caught rather than assumed. The live check is "},{"id":"spn-178965","marks":["code"],"text":"ln_0016"},{"id":"spn-178966","text":" in Travis's own world: retired with a reason, still readable, still counted, and refusing a new plan."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieran5cdvcu74l2lqblloe76whdhpcmnmfspxmxp4mar2sr67esjy6na","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}